@using Ecnanib.DecisionEngine

@*
    What a check of the Risk Guard computed and asked, as a page shows it: the size of the order
    of a plan that opens a position (FR-RSK-5), and every rule with its outcome and why, in plain
    language and with the numbers (FR-RSK-9, NFR-USA-2). The page of the risk checks of an agent
    shows it for each check, and the timeline of a cycle for the checks of that cycle (FR-CYC-10).
    An outcome is said as words, and does not rely on a colour. The texts are in RiskCheckPages.
*@

@* The size that the check computed for the order of a plan that opens a position (FR-RSK-5). *@
@if (RiskCheckPages.Sized(Check) is { } sized)
{
    <p class="guard-size">@sized</p>
}

@*
    The table scrolls by itself on a narrow screen, also by keyboard, as the list of agents does.
    It is named by the heading of its check, as the part around it is: a page shows one table
    for each check, and the caption, which all of them share, would tell none apart (NFR-USA-1).
    The caption is read out after the name, as what the table holds.
*@
<div class="agents risk-check-rules" role="region" aria-labelledby="@LabelledBy" tabindex="0">
    <table aria-labelledby="@LabelledBy">
        <caption>@RiskCheckPages.RulesCaption</caption>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">@RiskCheckPages.RuleHeading</th>
                <th scope="col">@RiskCheckPages.OutcomeHeading</th>
                <th scope="col">@RiskCheckPages.WhyHeading</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var rule in Check.Rules)
            {
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">@RiskCheckPages.NameOf(rule.Rule)</th>
                    <td><span class="rule-outcome rule-@(rule.Outcome.ToString().ToLowerInvariant())">@RiskCheckPages.Describe(rule.Outcome)</span></td>
                    <td>@RiskCheckPages.Says(rule, Check.Action, Check.Kind)</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The check.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RiskCheckView Check { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>
    /// The id of the heading that names the check, which the table is read out under. Where a
    /// page shows the checks of several decisions, the id of the heading of the decision stands
    /// before it, so no two tables of a page have one name.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string LabelledBy { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
